---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url.js';
---
<Base title="About" description="Engineer moving from civil and structural engineering in energy into product design and design strategy.">
  <div class="page about">
    <header>
      <p class="corner">02 &mdash; Who this is</p>
      <h1 class="script about__title">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="about__grid">
      <div class="prose about__body">
        <p class="lede lede--small">
          I am an engineer. I spent four years in energy infrastructure and I am now
          moving into product design and design strategy.
        </p>

        <p>
          I studied Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering at UCL, and then
          joined Mott MacDonald, working across Seoul and London. The first half was
          renewable energy — offshore wind substructures at gigawatt scale, solar
          projects between 20 and 110 MW. The second half was new-build nuclear.
        </p>

        <p>
          The work I was best at was rarely the calculation. It was translation:
          turning an ambiguous client requirement into something a team could build
          against, turning a technical constraint into a decision a stakeholder could
          take, helping peer reviewers and regulators agree on what counted as
          evidence. That is design work; in engineering it is not usually called
          that.
        </p>

        <p>
          I moved on because of what the work optimised for. Cost and programme are real
          constraints and I am not sentimental about them, but a solution can satisfy
          both and still be disconnected from the people it reaches. That gap is rarely
          anyone's responsibility in the process, and I would rather work somewhere it
          is.
        </p>

        <p>
          I start Harvard's Master in Design Engineering in August 2026.
        </p>

        <h2>Two baselines</h2>

        <p>
          I am a dual Korean and British citizen and native in both languages, which
          is most useful to me as a point of comparison. My dissertation started because
          Korean bus signage is denser and easier to scan than London's, and the reason
          turned out to be structural rather than a matter of taste: Korean characters
          need less horizontal space, so more information fits at the same legibility.
          Having a second reference point is how I notice problems in the first one.
        </p>

        <h2>What I am not claiming</h2>

        <p>
          Nothing in this portfolio has shipped to users. All four projects sit at
          concept, analysis or MVP-draft stage, and they are presented here as
          investigations rather than products. The Patchwork MVP was vibe-coded rather
          than hand-built. I am working through CS50 in C separately, and this site is
          the first thing here I built by hand.
        </p>

        <p>
          My habit of defining the frame early is a strength once a project is moving,
          and less helpful in the divergent stage, where the frame can arrive before
          enough options do. I am working on holding it open longer.
        </p>

        <h2>Outside</h2>

        <p>
          Basketball, photography, creative writing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="about__side">
        <div class="about__card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Looking for</p>
          <p>Product Design Engineer, Design Technologist, and Hardware / Systems Design Engineer roles.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about__card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Based</p>
          <p>London and Seoul. Cambridge, MA from August 2026.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about__card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Languages</p>
          <p>English and Korean, both native.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about__card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
          <p><a href="mailto:elina_lee@mde.harvard.edu">elina_lee@mde.harvard.edu</a></p>
          <p class="meta">TODO(elina): LinkedIn / GitHub</p>
        </div>
        <p><a href={href('/cv/')}>Full CV &rarr;</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: var(--space-8); }
  .about__title {
    font-size: clamp(var(--size-8), 9vw, var(--size-10));
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-7);
  }
  .about__grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-8); }
  @media (min-width: 950px) {
    .about__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 260px; gap: var(--space-10); }
  }
  .about__body h2 {
    font-size: var(--size-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--border-hair) solid var(--rule);
  }
  .about__side { display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); align-content: start; font-size: var(--size-2); }
  .about__card { border-top: var(--border-mark) solid var(--ink); padding-top: var(--space-3); }
  .about__card p + p { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
</style>
